1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,990
And you just stand there, filming with
that damn camera.

2
00:00:03,633 --> 00:00:05,313
Do you think that camera is you?

3
00:00:06,450 --> 00:00:11,200
Don't Cut Me Into Your Film

4
00:00:11,967 --> 00:00:12,400
Let's run the lines.

5
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:13,240
I must see you.

6
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,900
Fuck off. Stop tormenting me.

7
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:16,700
I love you.

8
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:17,567
That was terrible acting.

9
00:00:17,567 --> 00:00:19,917
You have to really love him,

10
00:00:20,397 --> 00:00:25,767
Not for real. You're acting. You're
pretending.

11
00:00:25,767 --> 00:00:26,533
It's the same.

12
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:35,733
They're both broken, trying to reconnect.
But the pieces won't fit.

13
00:00:35,733 --> 00:00:37,467
They only cut each other.

14
00:00:37,467 --> 00:00:38,417
Understand?

15
00:00:38,433 --> 00:00:39,253
Hmm.

16
00:00:39,267 --> 00:00:45,657
Yes, you can imagine your skin, your soul
is made of fragments, and very sharp.

17
00:00:45,667 --> 00:00:48,497
Put us together shaking, shaking, shaking,

18
00:00:48,547 --> 00:00:51,737
Put us in a big plastic bag and shake it.

19
00:00:51,907 --> 00:00:52,067
Hmm.

20
00:00:52,067 --> 00:00:53,467
We only break into smaller pieces.

21
00:00:53,987 --> 00:00:56,800
There's no way for either of us to save
the other.

22
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:58,040
Why don't they just split up?

23
00:00:58,190 --> 00:00:58,667
Just split up.

24
00:00:58,667 --> 00:01:00,387
Isn't this art?

25
00:01:00,387 --> 00:01:01,467
[laughter]

26
00:01:01,467 --> 00:01:02,977
All that explaining for nothing.

27
00:01:03,633 --> 00:01:05,533
this is not love, understand?

28
00:01:05,613 --> 00:01:08,233
This is not love, this is, I don't know
what to call it, but...

29
00:01:08,233 --> 00:01:10,220
It's worse than the love I imagine. A
hundred times worse.

30
00:01:10,233 --> 00:01:11,033
Do you understand?

31
00:01:11,033 --> 00:01:11,393
I mean...

32
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:12,160
I understand.

33
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:14,667
you're not listening to me at all. Not at
all.

34
00:01:14,667 --> 00:01:16,147
How many times do I have to tell you?

35
00:01:16,147 --> 00:01:19,827
After so many rehearsals, You still can't
get this simple bit right?

36
00:01:19,827 --> 00:01:20,067
I mean...

37
00:01:20,733 --> 00:01:22,267
you don't have that feeling.

38
00:01:22,267 --> 00:01:24,347
You always say okay, "I know. I
understand."

39
00:01:24,347 --> 00:01:26,387
But you don't believe me.

40
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:28,360
You just don't get it.

41
00:01:28,367 --> 00:01:30,033
You have to look into his eyes, and tell
him...

42
00:01:30,033 --> 00:01:31,953
I've lost patience with this play.

43
00:01:31,967 --> 00:01:33,633
How long will this drag on?

44
00:01:33,633 --> 00:01:35,553
"Desperate joy." "Resolve in collapse."

45
00:01:35,553 --> 00:01:36,233
What words?

46
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:37,553
How the fuck do I act that?

47
00:01:37,567 --> 00:01:40,900
I'm thinking... Where do we begin, and
where do we end?

48
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:41,500
Think about it.

49
00:01:41,980 --> 00:01:42,750
Let me think.

50
00:01:42,767 --> 00:01:43,600
At the beginning...

51
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:47,067
Or in your script, how does it begin and
end?

52
00:01:47,067 --> 00:01:48,267
You're destroying me.

53
00:01:48,277 --> 00:01:51,367
It begins with destruction. When I realize
you're destroying me.

54
00:01:51,367 --> 00:01:53,897
And it ends when I'm destroyed. Then you
sleep peacefully.

55
00:01:54,137 --> 00:01:56,817
You're cold. So cold. until you freeze to
death.

56
00:01:56,833 --> 00:01:59,723
It's bleak. A bleak beginning and ending.

57
00:01:59,733 --> 00:02:03,333
And... We can just act naturally. It
doesn't have to feel like theatre.

58
00:02:03,333 --> 00:02:04,703
I understand, I know, It's not theatre.

59
00:02:04,703 --> 00:02:08,643
Well, in everyday life... but daily life
also has emotions, and violence.

60
00:02:08,863 --> 00:02:09,467
Ah. Yes.

61
00:02:09,467 --> 00:02:13,500
When you see someone you like, you want to
smile. Yes.

62
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:14,767
Not that often.

63
00:02:14,767 --> 00:02:16,567
I don't feel like you're destroying me.

64
00:02:16,567 --> 00:02:19,283
A habit. A habit of what? Hurting others.

65
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:19,460
Hmm.

66
00:02:19,467 --> 00:02:24,133
Because that, I wrote it when I was in a
bad mood. I'm in a good mood now.

67
00:02:24,133 --> 00:02:30,900
Maybe we don't have to hurt each other.
Just play a tender, helpless love.

68
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:31,780
I'm getting into it.

69
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:33,367
Okay. Give me a moment.

70
00:02:33,367 --> 00:02:36,133
Can you see me without your glasses?

71
00:02:36,133 --> 00:02:38,093
Can you see me like this?

72
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:41,733
I can see you. And everything around you
has a soft halo.

73
00:02:41,733 --> 00:02:43,817
Am I blurry then? You're not blurry.

74
00:02:43,927 --> 00:02:45,827
Everything around you gets blurry.

75
00:02:45,947 --> 00:02:49,573
Is there light around me? Yes. Is there?

76
00:02:50,233 --> 00:02:52,867
Look again, is there light?

77
00:02:52,867 --> 00:02:54,627
Maybe. There's light in your eyes.

78
00:02:55,227 --> 00:02:57,933
What about around me? Beside me...

79
00:02:57,933 --> 00:02:59,083
The light is in your eyes.

80
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:02,367
But you're not looking into my eyes.

81
00:03:02,367 --> 00:03:03,487
Are you looking?

82
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:05,520
My eyes are here.

83
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:08,710
Am I hallucinating?

84
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:10,460
Hahaha.

85
00:03:10,467 --> 00:03:11,933
Are you hallucinating?

86
00:03:11,933 --> 00:03:14,000
There's this person. His name is He Fa.

87
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:21,160
He kept saying he wanted everyone to
understand each other.

88
00:03:21,167 --> 00:03:26,000
He said honest communication mattered
most.

89
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:31,633
But when I said I wanted to talk honestly
with him, he refused. Hmm.

90
00:03:31,633 --> 00:03:34,263
I thought he was such a hypocrite. Why did
he refuse?

91
00:03:34,343 --> 00:03:35,253
How did he refuse?

92
00:03:35,893 --> 00:03:37,167
What actually happened?

93
00:03:37,167 --> 00:03:40,800
I think he might be a little afraid of me.

94
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:44,240
He's afraid. Yes. Like right now. He might
be a little afraid of me.

95
00:03:44,510 --> 00:03:47,000
Maybe I can make him angry too easily.

96
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,133
Afraid. Yes, afraid.

97
00:03:48,133 --> 00:03:51,223
I don't want anything to come between us.

98
00:03:51,867 --> 00:03:52,507
That's bullshit.

99
00:03:53,167 --> 00:03:56,407
Don't you hear how ridiculous that sounds?

100
00:03:57,067 --> 00:03:59,777
Huh?

101
00:04:00,287 --> 00:04:01,150
Why?

102
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:04,430
What do you mean, "come between us"?

103
00:04:04,830 --> 00:04:08,470
It already has.

104
00:04:09,133 --> 00:04:11,093
Didn't you say it was fine?

105
00:04:11,293 --> 00:04:12,213
What did I say?

106
00:04:12,867 --> 00:04:15,487
You think he'll come between us?

107
00:04:16,133 --> 00:04:21,227
Before... Hmm. Maybe I didn't think it
through before.

108
00:04:21,867 --> 00:04:25,427
But lately I've realized... He really has
affected us.

109
00:04:26,067 --> 00:04:29,247
You came to see me last night.

110
00:04:29,627 --> 00:04:29,973
Hmm.

111
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:33,530
I knew he'd changed something.

112
00:04:34,167 --> 00:04:37,757
I thought this would make you happy.

113
00:04:37,757 --> 00:04:45,180
When we first started... Wasn't it
because... It did make me happy at first.

114
00:04:45,833 --> 00:04:50,100
But now... What's changed?

115
00:04:50,733 --> 00:04:54,963
Maybe we were too optimistic at first. I
think so.

116
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:57,860
You think I should cut him off?

117
00:04:58,440 --> 00:05:06,540
I don't know. I just...

118
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:14,760
Hmm.

119
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:17,197
What are you going to do about him?

120
00:05:17,833 --> 00:05:20,153
I get jealous too, sometimes.

121
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:21,793
But I think I have to work through it.

122
00:05:22,433 --> 00:05:24,713
Are you afraid we'll break up?

123
00:05:25,367 --> 00:05:27,827
Probably. That's probably it.

124
00:05:28,467 --> 00:05:30,507
But I don't think we're that fragile.

125
00:05:31,167 --> 00:05:34,980
I mean... Our relationship shouldn't be
that fragile. No.

126
00:05:35,633 --> 00:05:36,943
What do you think?

127
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:40,110
What do you think?

128
00:05:40,430 --> 00:05:43,403
You... Don't you think a lot of things
have changed?

129
00:05:44,067 --> 00:05:47,167
You think the bad parts are things to
overcome.

130
00:05:47,833 --> 00:05:49,363
I can't do that anymore.

131
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,160
I can't get past it.

132
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:54,237
How... I don't know how to get past it.

133
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:57,270
I don't know why I have to work through
all this.

134
00:05:57,933 --> 00:05:59,733
It's strange. Why?

135
00:06:00,133 --> 00:06:05,140
Why let it get like this? It's a mess.

136
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,360
Do you want to end it?

137
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:10,983
So you're enjoying all this?

138
00:06:11,633 --> 00:06:12,673
Do you enjoy it?

139
00:06:12,833 --> 00:06:14,833
Why keep asking whether I accept it?

140
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:16,610
I'm not unhappy.

141
00:06:16,900 --> 00:06:21,047
You're happy? You're enjoying it? There's
more happiness than pain.

142
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:23,970
It's okay, I can listen to you, if you
want.

143
00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:25,580
Why is it always me who has to talk?

144
00:06:26,233 --> 00:06:28,263
Why am I always the one talking?

145
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:30,900
Can't you say something?

146
00:06:31,567 --> 00:06:37,893
You just stare at me, like this, and say
nothing. Not a damn word. Right?

147
00:06:38,533 --> 00:06:40,013
See? You're silent again.

148
00:06:40,653 --> 00:06:43,987
Maybe we should take a break, if you're
unhappy.

149
00:06:44,633 --> 00:06:47,623
So that's what you wanted to tell me? just
take a break.

150
00:06:48,183 --> 00:06:50,800
You thought about it all night, and this
is what you tell me?

151
00:06:51,467 --> 00:06:54,727
I don't know how to fix it. Maybe we can
stop.

152
00:06:55,367 --> 00:06:58,087
If this is hurting you, we can stop.

153
00:06:58,733 --> 00:07:04,803
I thought we'd find a way together to get
through this.

154
00:07:04,813 --> 00:07:18,043
But you're saying we should stop.

155
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:21,690
And you just stand there, filming with
that damn camera.

156
00:07:22,333 --> 00:07:24,013
Do you think that camera is you?

157
00:07:24,667 --> 00:07:24,897
Huh?

158
00:07:25,133 --> 00:07:27,373
You like watching me through it, right?

159
00:07:28,033 --> 00:07:33,873
Will you watch it at home and work out how
to answer me?

160
00:07:34,533 --> 00:07:35,603
I don't know what to do.

161
00:07:35,723 --> 00:07:37,693
I never thought we'd end up here.

162
00:07:38,333 --> 00:07:43,467
A way... What I'm trying to say is, we can
pause and think it through.

163
00:07:43,577 --> 00:07:46,687
But you need an answer from me right now.

164
00:07:47,333 --> 00:07:48,603
I don't have one.

165
00:07:49,267 --> 00:07:50,947
I don't know what's hurting you.

166
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:53,690
Everything hurts.

167
00:07:54,333 --> 00:07:56,593
I feel like I'm suffocating.

168
00:07:57,233 --> 00:07:57,993
Do you really understand?

169
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:02,840
I didn't get involved before because I
thought, "Not my fucking business."

170
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:05,760
But I know it's a mess. You think it's a
mess?

171
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:07,960
It is a mess. I admit it.

172
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:13,127
For me, in all this chaos, my main
responsibility is to record it.

173
00:08:13,133 --> 00:08:16,453
That's what I'm doing. But if I...

174
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:22,333
if I intervene, and become the person
responsible for keeping it safe,

175
00:08:22,333 --> 00:08:25,144
I'd make all this chaos clear.

176
00:08:25,293 --> 00:08:29,714
Turn it into something orderly and tightly
structured.

177
00:08:30,367 --> 00:08:32,720
And that would take it somewhere else.

178
00:08:32,790 --> 00:08:37,120
That place... that's where successful
people go.

179
00:08:37,133 --> 00:08:40,400
But I belong to the human surrender
faction.

180
00:08:41,033 --> 00:08:42,673
I don't want to do those things.

181
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:46,633
I feel responsible for humanity. So I have
to surrender,

182
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:48,860
I have to fail to the very end.

183
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:52,833
Stay in this chaos to the very end.

184
00:08:52,833 --> 00:08:57,673
Of course, until we finish filming this
piece.

185
00:08:58,333 --> 00:09:01,880
Then... it really will be the end.

186
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:05,220
This is my last breath. Last breath,

187
00:09:05,540 --> 00:09:08,900
Choose your words carefully. Is 'last
breath' really what you mean?

188
00:09:08,900 --> 00:09:12,100
I mean I'll see this through to the end.

189
00:09:12,540 --> 00:09:12,767
Hmm.

190
00:09:12,767 --> 00:09:16,097
I often wonder... why can't I love you?

191
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:18,830
No... no one taught us how to love.

192
00:09:18,867 --> 00:09:22,217
Can it be taught?

193
00:09:22,233 --> 00:09:23,703
Okay. You film. Okay.

194
00:09:24,193 --> 00:09:28,617
Let me set it up. It's already recording.
Just hold it.

195
00:09:28,633 --> 00:09:31,853
I'm a camera. I'm a camera.

196
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:34,720
Mm-hmm. Are you scared? Afraid of being
filmed?

197
00:09:35,367 --> 00:09:36,467
Of course not. Come closer.

198
00:09:36,467 --> 00:09:39,433
I'm a camera. Mm-hmm. Hello. I'm a camera.

199
00:09:39,433 --> 00:09:45,400
You're scared. You're resisting a camera.
How strange.

200
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:51,500
This time, who gets to call cut?

